# Observability (TypeScript)

Scaffolded by [ojiichan](https://gitlab.com/martin-wieser/ojiichan) to wire this
service into the same stack as the Python services: **ELK** structured events and
**__OJIICHAN_BACKEND__** (Sentry-compatible) error reporting.

## Install

```bash
npm install @sentry/node
```

`logEvent` uses the global `fetch` (Node 18+); no Elasticsearch client needed.

## Files

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `src/lib/config.ts` | Env-driven config (`OJIICHAN_<NAME>` first, then `<NAME>`). |
| `src/lib/sentry.ts` | `initSentry` / `captureException` / `flushSentry`. |
| `src/lib/elk.ts` | `logEvent` — one structured doc per event to ELK. |
| `src/handler-scaleway.ts` | `withObservability` wrapper for Scaleway functions. |

## Wiring

Initialize Sentry once at startup and report errors in your central handler
(e.g. `api.ts`):

```ts
import { initSentry, captureException } from "./lib/sentry";

initSentry();

// in your error handler / dispatch catch:
captureException(err, { route: req.path });
```

Emit structured events alongside errors:

```ts
import { logEvent } from "./lib/elk";

await logEvent(
  "matrix_exchange_failed",
  { operation: "matrix_exchange", error: String(err) },
  { level: "error", topic: "auth", failure: true },
);
```

For Scaleway Serverless Functions, wrap the exported handler so events flush
before the runtime freezes — see `src/handler-scaleway.ts`.

## Environment

| Variable | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `SENTRY_DSN` | __OJIICHAN_BACKEND__/Sentry ingest DSN. Unset ⇒ reporting no-ops. |
| `ENVIRONMENT` / `APP_ENV` | Deployment environment tag. |
| `RELEASE` / `GIT_COMMIT` | Release identifier. |
| `SERVICE_NAME` / `APP_NAME` | Logical service name. |
| `ELASTICSEARCH_HOST` | ELK host (with or without scheme). Unset ⇒ ELK no-ops. |
| `ELASTICSEARCH_PORT` | Defaults to `443`. |
| `ELASTICSEARCH_USERNAME` / `ELASTICSEARCH_PASSWORD` | Basic auth. |
| `ELASTICSEARCH_INDEX_PREFIX` | Index prefix; defaults to `app`. |

> **Self-signed ELK certs:** the global `fetch` validates TLS. For a self-signed
> cluster, run the service with a custom `undici` `Agent` (or, as a last resort,
> `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0`) — `ELASTICSEARCH_VERIFY_CERTS=false` documents
> intent but `fetch` does not read it.
